WEBVTT

00:09.870 --> 00:10.650
Arthur!

00:10.650 --> 00:11.740
Welcome home.

00:13.990 --> 00:16.160
How are your injuries? Are you okay?

00:16.160 --> 00:17.990
Everything all right?

00:20.420 --> 00:24.310
I'm so glad to see you home and safe.

00:24.870 --> 00:29.110
I'm sorry for always worrying you, Mom.

02:06.480 --> 02:11.500
#9 The King's Gratitude.

02:16.600 --> 02:17.470
That should do.

02:17.850 --> 02:19.300
Thanks, Mom.

02:19.910 --> 02:22.240
Now, you're next.

02:22.460 --> 02:24.270
Uh, but...

02:24.270 --> 02:25.990
Don't be shy, now.

02:25.990 --> 02:27.340
O-Okay.

02:35.940 --> 02:37.900
<i>A powerful Emitter,</i>

02:39.160 --> 02:43.910
<i>and an AA-ranked adventurer, 
the former leader of the Twinhorns.</i>

02:48.140 --> 02:49.270
What's wrong?

02:50.100 --> 02:52.580
I think I understand part 
of how you're so strong.

02:53.020 --> 02:55.520
You've got an incredible pair of parents.

02:57.400 --> 02:58.280
Right?

02:59.010 --> 02:59.870
Right?!

03:02.060 --> 03:04.020
I'm honestly jealous.

03:16.070 --> 03:17.510
All right, we're heading out.

03:17.850 --> 03:18.920
We'll be back.

03:18.920 --> 03:21.530
Me, too!

03:20.260 --> 03:21.530
Not today.

03:21.530 --> 03:23.690
How come?

03:23.150 --> 03:25.450
The boys need some time to themselves.

03:23.690 --> 03:26.030
I wanna go, too!

03:42.320 --> 03:45.020
Okay, let's go over today's quest.

03:45.410 --> 03:46.390
What are our objectives?

03:46.950 --> 03:49.330
Picking up my essential supplies.

03:49.830 --> 03:51.100
And our conditions for finishing?

03:51.520 --> 03:53.330
Staying under budget.

03:54.010 --> 03:56.340
Sounds good, Elijah. I should've known.

03:56.780 --> 03:59.450
And you're sure this is all right?

03:59.450 --> 04:01.910
I said the same thing about 
getting into the academy,

04:01.910 --> 04:04.090
but you're really doing 
too to much care for me.

04:04.310 --> 04:09.390
It's fine, and only natural, 
considering you saved my life.

04:09.390 --> 04:12.980
When you put it that way, I need to 
figure a way to pay you back, too.

04:13.830 --> 04:15.480
If it weren't for you,

04:15.480 --> 04:18.580
{I would've }they would've found my corpse at 
the bottom of that labyrinth, too.

04:19.660 --> 04:20.760
Elijah...

04:22.380 --> 04:26.620
Okay then, how about you work 
for me until you die, then?

04:26.900 --> 04:27.960
Hey!

04:27.960 --> 04:29.920
I'm just joking. Now, come on.

04:31.390 --> 04:32.870
Wait!

04:33.120 --> 04:34.810
No, seriously, wait!

04:34.810 --> 04:39.310
I don't know my way around town! 
Are you trying to get me lost?!

04:55.490 --> 04:56.070
Here.

05:01.300 --> 05:03.070
Looks like your injuries have healed.

05:03.460 --> 05:05.150
Yeah. Sorry.

05:05.410 --> 05:06.720
Don't do that.

05:08.130 --> 05:10.950
Thank you for waiting until I was healed.

05:13.860 --> 05:17.540
It's okay. This next quest is 
looking a little on the tough side,

05:17.540 --> 05:20.170
so I'm better off going with you.

05:22.000 --> 05:24.220
If you have something to say,
 you need to say it.

05:26.020 --> 05:31.170
Could we wait a little bit before leaving?
 There's something I want to do.

05:31.920 --> 05:32.750
Okay.

05:33.140 --> 05:34.180
Are you sure?

05:34.570 --> 05:37.390
Do you realize how long we've 
been in a party together?

05:37.760 --> 05:41.040
It's obvious to me what my cute 
surrogate sister is thinking.

05:49.690 --> 05:51.660
I can't see in front of me.

05:51.660 --> 05:53.700
Okay, next is...

05:53.970 --> 05:56.710
Arthur, this is enough.

05:57.600 --> 05:59.220
Let's take a break, then.

06:03.870 --> 06:05.840
I feel alive again.

06:06.190 --> 06:07.970
Don't exaggerate.

06:08.230 --> 06:10.920
Maybe you should carry 
some of this stuff, then.

06:10.920 --> 06:12.950
Why not use your dimension ring?

06:15.470 --> 06:17.350
Good point!

06:17.350 --> 06:20.300
You can really be absent-minded 
at times, Elijah.

06:21.560 --> 06:23.200
What do you like more:
 apples or pears?

06:23.200 --> 06:24.230
Apples.

06:24.230 --> 06:24.940
I think pears?

06:24.940 --> 06:27.790
Yeah, I'd go with pears too.

06:27.790 --> 06:29.570
I know, right!

06:35.240 --> 06:36.090
Let's go.

06:36.450 --> 06:37.080
Yeah.

06:44.000 --> 06:46.260
Give me the info on Note.

06:48.760 --> 06:50.920
Hey! Are you listening to me?

06:52.760 --> 06:54.030
You bastard...

06:54.910 --> 06:57.850
You think a mere guild head can oppose me?

06:59.210 --> 07:02.710
With the three-kingdom alliance, 
the adventurer's guild

07:02.710 --> 07:04.950
is now active internationally, 
accepting other races,

07:04.950 --> 07:07.900
which has meant a tightening of our rules.

07:08.880 --> 07:13.410
Do not assume that being a Wykes affords 
you the same privileges it once did.

07:13.840 --> 07:15.020
What'd you just say?

07:15.480 --> 07:18.160
You're not even an 
adventurer at the moment.

07:18.610 --> 07:23.170
Do you really think I'll bow
to the whims of a civilian?

07:25.500 --> 07:28.270
Damn it! This isn't over.

07:29.990 --> 07:33.180
Damn it, damn it, damn it...

07:33.600 --> 07:34.740
Sir...

07:34.740 --> 07:40.680
Making a mockery of me. 
This all his... Note's fault!

07:40.960 --> 07:42.390
Calm down, please.

07:42.390 --> 07:43.810
Shut up! We're heading back!

07:43.810 --> 07:44.560
Yes, sir!

07:44.800 --> 07:46.590
But what about Shiun?

07:46.590 --> 07:47.720
Don't care.

07:47.720 --> 07:49.500
Sir!

07:57.790 --> 08:00.260
No pertinent information, it seems.

08:05.580 --> 08:08.510
Jasmine Flamesworth.

08:09.830 --> 08:13.420
A member of the Twinhorns, eh?

08:26.400 --> 08:27.900
<i>What's that?</i>

08:27.900 --> 08:29.510
<i>It's not food.</i>

08:29.510 --> 08:31.360
<i>But I'm hungry.</i>

08:32.270 --> 08:34.860
<i>And I smell something good.</i>

08:35.530 --> 08:36.350
<i>You mean this?</i>

08:36.350 --> 08:37.370
<i>That's it!</i>

08:47.800 --> 08:50.540
<i>Don't be mean! Let me eat it already!</i>

08:50.540 --> 08:53.630
<i>That's not happening. 
I'm still studying it.</i>

08:54.420 --> 08:57.640
What I'm really stuck on
 is what to do with this.

09:01.050 --> 09:03.250
Arthur, Daddy's calling you.

09:03.250 --> 09:05.640
Okay. Thanks, Eleanor.

09:05.640 --> 09:07.950
You're very welcome!

09:17.210 --> 09:18.100
Jasmine?

09:18.900 --> 09:21.410
Jasmine and the others are setting out.

09:23.280 --> 09:27.620
This next quest is a fair bit away. 
I won't see you again for a while.

09:28.040 --> 09:29.250
I see.

09:29.950 --> 09:31.800
<i>I expected as much.</i>

09:32.230 --> 09:36.210
<i>This was bound to happen
once I stopped being Note.</i>

09:37.190 --> 09:38.130
Arthur.

09:39.960 --> 09:43.310
One last bit of training. Fight me.

09:56.620 --> 09:58.350
Good luck, you two.

09:58.350 --> 10:01.070
Don't lose, Arthur!

10:01.070 --> 10:04.290
Uh, wait, why exactly are they fighting?

10:04.850 --> 10:06.830
It's kind of an adventurer tradition.

10:07.280 --> 10:09.620
No matter how much your 
mana core has strengthened,

10:09.620 --> 10:11.390
there's more to a fight than that.

10:11.720 --> 10:15.710
Mistakes in judgment and moments of 
carelessness can still cost you your life.

10:16.660 --> 10:19.310
Even if you're AA-ranked.

10:21.520 --> 10:25.100
The only way to truly take someone's 
measure is to fight them.

10:25.330 --> 10:28.280
Jasmine, we'll put up a barrier.

10:28.280 --> 10:30.600
Don't hold back, Arthur.

10:31.930 --> 10:33.360
Are you ready?

10:35.700 --> 10:38.360
<i>That look in her eyes takes me back.</i>

10:42.070 --> 10:44.970
<i>To the way she looked in those 
days when we would risk our lives,</i>

10:44.970 --> 10:47.420
<i>fighting like warriors. Which means...</i>

10:49.150 --> 10:50.390
I'm going all out.

10:51.930 --> 10:52.770
Understood.

10:54.870 --> 10:55.800
Begin!

11:46.780 --> 11:50.980
<i>These two years as an adventurer have 
allowed me to hone my sword skills.</i>

11:51.520 --> 11:56.510
<i>I'm still not on par with my past life, 
but I will show her how I've improved.</i>

12:10.280 --> 12:12.750
They're fighting in 
Jasmine's preferred range.

12:13.070 --> 12:14.850
That'd be rough, even for Adam.

12:14.850 --> 12:17.150
I wouldn't let her get that close.

12:17.500 --> 12:19.760
Jasmine is really going for it.

12:19.760 --> 12:23.400
I don't know about that. I think 
they're still getting warmed up.

12:29.840 --> 12:31.270
<i>I need to keep my distance.</i>

12:32.500 --> 12:33.770
<i>She predicted what I'd do.</i>

12:47.370 --> 12:48.430
Good choice.

12:48.780 --> 12:50.510
I wouldn't be so sure.

12:50.990 --> 12:53.290
We ended up fighting in your range.

12:53.850 --> 12:56.790
Making a mistake isn't a problem.

12:57.060 --> 12:59.450
As long you know know how 
make up from the mistake.

12:59.810 --> 13:02.300
That's how you manage to survive.

13:03.050 --> 13:03.830
That's right.

13:05.080 --> 13:06.510
I'm sorry, Jasmine.

13:07.150 --> 13:09.300
But I don't think I can 
beat you with just a sword.

13:12.540 --> 13:15.750
It's okay. Let's start using magic, too.

13:24.270 --> 13:29.070
Arthur had told me about his mana core's 
growth, but this is still impressive.

13:29.070 --> 13:32.950
And he's only 11. He's going 
to be a terror in the future.

13:33.400 --> 13:36.710
He's way stronger than 
when I fought him before.

13:45.150 --> 13:46.830
Thanks for that, Durden.

13:46.830 --> 13:49.970
No problem. But we should 
maybe back up a bit more.

13:50.960 --> 13:51.880
Wow.

13:55.870 --> 14:01.440
<i>She boosts her output at the moment of
defense. That's a trick I can't manage yet.</i>

14:02.420 --> 14:04.520
<i>I'll just have to pry her guard open.</i>

14:16.450 --> 14:17.780
Whoa, whoa!

14:17.780 --> 14:19.990
Controlling that much fire...

14:19.990 --> 14:21.880
That's as much fire as Lucas!

14:38.880 --> 14:40.540
That's going overboard!

14:40.540 --> 14:42.270
It's really impressive.

14:42.270 --> 14:44.770
And definitely on par 
with AA-rank firepower.

14:48.830 --> 14:50.570
<i>She neutralized it.</i>

14:51.410 --> 14:54.030
How in the world?

14:54.480 --> 14:57.040
By dispersing it with equal force.

14:57.280 --> 15:00.040
She dispersed it?! 
But that seems impossible!

15:00.370 --> 15:02.760
Jasmine is a Flamesworth,

15:02.760 --> 15:06.050
the family that wields the most powerful 
fire magic in the kingdom of Sapin.

15:06.050 --> 15:09.290
Fire magic? But...

15:09.750 --> 15:12.660
She was born with an affinity for wind.

15:13.020 --> 15:14.320
But that's the only difference.

15:14.890 --> 15:17.650
She's still a member of the 
most powerful mage bloodline.

15:18.900 --> 15:22.310
It's taken a toll on 
her self-esteem, but...

15:22.860 --> 15:27.720
I'd say these two years with Arthur 
have been valuable for Jasmine, too.

15:37.080 --> 15:38.870
What amazing wind.

15:41.510 --> 15:46.160
I remember what you said the first time 
I showed it to you. Which is why....

15:49.670 --> 15:51.020
I want you to get serious!

15:51.680 --> 15:53.380
<i>I already was.</i>

15:54.230 --> 15:55.360
Okay.

15:57.630 --> 15:58.890
I'll use this next.

16:14.190 --> 16:16.280
<i>Touching her with my 
blade will mean victory.</i>

16:16.660 --> 16:18.150
<i>She'll be forced to dodge.</i>

16:18.620 --> 16:19.740
<i>So I have to press her!</i>

16:25.400 --> 16:28.380
<i>Compressing air to block it 
without making contact, eh?</i>

16:34.020 --> 16:35.480
Don't repeat the same tactics.

16:49.630 --> 16:53.200
She's predicting my moves. 
Nothing is working.

16:54.360 --> 16:57.690
What do I do? What do I do?

17:15.260 --> 17:16.420
<i>I won't use that.</i>

17:18.980 --> 17:25.940
<i>She didn't just teach me how to 
use a sword, but how to survive.</i>

17:26.540 --> 17:30.980
<i>She gave me the strength I'll need to 
always return to the people I care for.</i>

17:32.410 --> 17:34.940
The fight's just getting started, Jasmine.

17:35.900 --> 17:38.470
That's fine by me, Arthur.

17:45.130 --> 17:46.260
It's just some powder.

17:46.260 --> 17:47.080
Oh, no—

17:51.910 --> 17:52.590
<i>Oil!</i>

18:02.270 --> 18:04.220
I have you now, Jasmine!

18:08.230 --> 18:09.750
What is this?

18:12.620 --> 18:14.130
Did she really...

18:14.980 --> 18:17.210
Don't worry. You won't die.

18:18.620 --> 18:20.520
You'll just be numb for a while.

18:22.510 --> 18:25.250
Okay. All the stops, then.

18:31.480 --> 18:35.740
<i>Not to win, or kill, but to survive.</i>

18:37.190 --> 18:41.080
<i>She taught me what I needed 
to know to do just that.</i>

18:44.720 --> 18:49.790
<i>So I have to win, to show her. 
By using everything she caught me...</i>

18:51.110 --> 18:52.830
<i>Show her I'll be fine.</i>

18:54.650 --> 18:57.310
<i>And that I can move forward on my own.</i>

18:58.050 --> 18:59.220
Jasmine!

19:22.060 --> 19:24.230
You come up with the sneakiest ideas.

19:25.700 --> 19:27.930
Just like how you taught me.

19:29.730 --> 19:32.050
You've gotten stronger, Arthur.

19:36.470 --> 19:37.520
Thank you.

19:45.830 --> 19:47.450
Here, Jasmine.

19:52.610 --> 19:54.010
A dimension ring?

19:54.010 --> 19:56.470
Yeah. My thanks for the past two years.

19:57.650 --> 19:58.760
Thank you.

19:59.090 --> 20:01.340
Tell me about what happened 
when you get back.

20:01.600 --> 20:05.850
Yeah. I want you to tell 
me about the academy, too.

20:06.420 --> 20:08.760
All right. It's a promise.

20:09.110 --> 20:10.240
It's a promise.

20:19.220 --> 20:20.100
What's wrong?

20:23.090 --> 20:24.860
<i>This isn't like me.</i>

20:25.420 --> 20:29.360
<i>I see them, and find myself 
projecting my own wishes.</i>

20:30.590 --> 20:33.160
<i>What if he hadn't run back then?</i>

20:33.820 --> 20:35.670
<i>What if I had been more forgiving?</i>

20:36.920 --> 20:39.170
<i>What if, what if...</i>

20:41.160 --> 20:43.370
<i>I find myself asking the same kinds 
of questions, but ultimately...</i>

21:01.710 --> 21:02.850
Say, Elijah...

21:03.920 --> 21:07.090
Do you think the three of us 
could've become like them?

21:09.820 --> 21:10.840
It's too late now.

21:11.950 --> 21:12.880
I know.

21:14.100 --> 21:17.340
<i>But it leaves me feeling a bit sad.</i>
